      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since iPhoneOS 3.1 the app binaries store binding data in the LC_DYLD_INFO command, and leave the external relocations empty in the DYSYMTAB. Simply dumping all symbols and their offsets from DYLD_INFO into the external relocations map does the trick and greatly improves compatibility with 3.1+ (together with https://review.gerrithub.io/c/touchHLE/touchHLE/+/1213534 they go way past the usual crashing point and start to actually load), but non-lazy symbols are handled twice in this case, and DYLD_INFO could potentially contain more information that might need to be handled, most notably the rebase commands (we already handle weak binds). I am still yet to see a binary that does, though.",
